      "kind": "default",
      "html": "<p><strong>1. Who does the write-up.</strong> With SafetyCulture, the person on the job fills in the app on site, and the report is only as finished as what they typed. With Quickler, they talk or send photos as they go, and Quickler writes the report from that. Ethos Safety put it this way on LinkedIn: <a class=\"graeme-link\" href=\"/graeme/\" title=\"Read Graeme's story\">\"The report develops during the inspection, reducing the need to reconstruct the visit from a collection of notes afterwards.\"</a></p><p><strong>2. How the person on the job answers.</strong> SafetyCulture: they open its app and work through a form. Quickler: they message in WhatsApp by text, voice note or photo, in any order. Quickler sorts each answer into the right question and asks only about what is still missing.</p><p><strong>3. Whose report you get.</strong> SafetyCulture gives you its report from its own templates. Quickler fills in your own report: send the Word or PDF report you already issue and every new Record comes back in that layout. We have not found SafetyCulture saying whether it can fill a firm's own existing layout, so we do not claim it cannot.</p>",
